### Security Guidelines
- **Sanitize User Input**: Always escape special HTML characters in user input to prevent XSS attacks. Use a helper function like `escape_html` to convert characters such as `<`, `>`, `&`, `"`, and `'` into their corresponding HTML entities.

Example:
```cpp
std::string escape_html(const std::string &input) {
    std::string escaped;
    for (char c : input) {
        switch(c) {
            case '<':  escaped += "&lt;"; break;
            case '>':  escaped += "&gt;"; break;
            case '&':  escaped += "&amp;"; break;
            case '"':  escaped += "&quot;"; break;
            case '\'': escaped += "&#39;"; break;
            default:   escaped += c; break;
        }
    }
    return escaped;
}
```

Then, in your function:
```cpp
std::string get_welcome_message(const std::string &username) {
    return "Welcome, " + escape_html(username) + "!";
}
```


